# Build context is the REPO ROOT (the Dockerfile COPYs both agenticRAG/ and
# config/, which have no common parent below it). That makes the context large
# by default — .vrm models, node_modules, the 465 MB local ONNX export — and
# every byte of it is uploaded to the builder before the first instruction runs.
#
# On CI that upload is the slowest part of a build whose whole point is a fast
# feedback loop, so this file matters more than it looks.

# Version control and IDE
.git
.github
.claude
.vscode
.idea

# The ONNX export. Reproduced INSIDE the image by the export stage — shipping
# the local copy would upload 465 MB to build a file the builder makes itself.
models/

# Frontend: nothing in the image reads it
ECA_UI/
text-to-motion/
SpeechLLm/

# ...except the shared motion job module. agenticRAG/Dockerfile COPYs
# text-to-motion/kimodo/vva_motion into the image, because the Lambda and the
# GPU worker must agree byte-for-byte on the job id and the table schema, and
# the Kimodo image's build context (text-to-motion/kimodo) cannot reach up to a
# shared location. The exclusion above hid it and the build died with
#
#   failed to compute cache key: "/text-to-motion/kimodo/vva_motion": not found
#
# after both test gates had passed — the last place this could still break.
# Both lines are needed: the first re-admits the directory entry, the second its
# contents. Everything else under text-to-motion/ stays excluded, which is the
# point: DART alone once filled a runner's disk.
# Guarded by tests/infra/test_dockerignore_allows_copied_paths.py.
!text-to-motion/kimodo/vva_motion
!text-to-motion/kimodo/vva_motion/**

# Infrastructure and docs
infra/
docs/
scripts/
tests/
data/
logs/

# Python artefacts
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/*.egg-info/
**/.venv/
**/venv/

# Local state that must never reach an image
**/.env
**/.env.local
*.log
*.db
*.sqlite3

# The voices directory is TTS-only, and TTS is off on this image
voices/
